DMbot - TESTING HISTORY (append-only)
=====================================
The complete record of live tests, newest at the bottom. Entries are added, never
rewritten (corrections go in a new dated entry). The current picture is in
docs/testing-status.log. Maintained by the PyCharm session. Never put tokens, .env
contents or players' personal data here (the repo is public).

==============================================================================
2026-10-04  Test 1, run 1: voice capture, no transcription (DM only)
==============================================================================
Runbook     docs/LIVE_TEST.md, Test 1 (from branch docs/live-test-runbook at the time)
Commit      development @ e40e3de
Machine     Windows 11 Home 10.0.26200; Node 22.23.2; npm 10.9.8;
            Python 3.12.14 (conda env "dmbot")
Settings    TRANSCRIBER=none
Speakers    1 (the DM). No second person in this run.
Channel     "General Voice"; DM updates in #dm-screen

Setup
  - core's first start exited: "Transcription problem: Local Whisper is not installed."
    Cause: TRANSCRIBER had the wrong value in .env (the owner's mistake, since fixed).
    Not a bug; the runbook's hint for this error was correct.
  - core started:
      INFO dmbot.ears.server: Waiting for ears on ws://127.0.0.1:8765
      WARNING discord.client: PyNaCl is not installed, voice will NOT be supported   (-> #38)
      WARNING discord.client: davey is not installed, voice will NOT be supported    (-> #38)
  - ears: npm ci (92 packages), then npm run dev:
      [ears] logged in as DMbot#4185
      [ears] connected to core
    core: "ears connected"

Discord (pasted by the owner; times are the owner's local time)
  02:48  /table status -> Voice service: connected ✅ / Table: not listening /
         Opted in: nobody yet / Transcription: 0 waiting
  02:48  /table join -> "Joining General Voice. Updates for the DM will appear in this
         channel, so keep it private to you."
  02:48  #dm-screen: "✅ Listening in General Voice. 0 player(s) have opted in to recording."
  02:48  /table status -> Table: General Voice (listening), DM @DM / Opted in: nobody yet
  02:50  /consent give -> "Thanks — DMbot will now transcribe your voice..."
  02:50  /table status -> Opted in: DM / Transcription: 0 waiting, last delay 0.0 s (-> #39)
  02:50-02:51  Capture checks:
         1. DM — 1 × speech, 2.6 s, audio 100%
         2. DM — 1 × speech, 13.9 s, audio 91% ⚠️ audio gaps
         3. DM — 2 × speech, 7.1 s, audio 100%
         4. DM — 3 × speech, 12.9 s, audio 91% ⚠️ audio gaps
         5. DM — 3 × speech, 11.0 s, audio 94% ⚠️ audio gaps
         6. DM — 3 × speech, 4.9 s, audio 100%
  02:51  /table leave -> "Stopped listening. 👋"

Terminals during the session
  No errors, tracebacks or "Could not post" warnings. Nothing was logged after
  "ears connected", because session events aren't logged (-> #37).

Results (LIVE_TEST.md step 5)
  Both parts connected, bot online ...... PASS
  Join messages ......................... PASS for #dm-screen; voice-chat notice inferred
                                          (no "weren't told" warning, no post failure logged)
  Audio % per speaker ................... BORDERLINE (two at 91%, one at 94%)
  Every consenting speaker appears ...... PASS (1 of 1)
  Revoked speaker disappears ............ NOT TESTED (needs a second person)
  No errors in either terminal .......... PASS
  Overall ............................... PARTIAL / BORDERLINE

Analysis
  Low % only on long speech. Clients send Opus silence frames and then stop during
  pauses; ears counted pauses under 800 ms as lost frames.

Issues filed: #36 (audio pauses counted as loss), #37, #38, #39. Tracking issue: #40.

Follow-up
  - #36 fixed in PR #46 (merged to development @ 0c7f9d9, CI green). Health is now
    tracked per Opus packet; a gap after 3+ silence frames counts as a pause.
    DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1 logs per-utterance health.
  - Review follow-ups: #43 (DAVE loss right after a pause), #44 ("95% ⚠️" rounding),
    #45 (decode errors and link drops not counted).
  - Run 2 needs a second person, DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1, and ideally ~5% injected loss.

==============================================================================
2026-10-05  Cloud test server set up (no test run)
==============================================================================
Machine     Ubuntu 26.04 LTS VM, 4 vCPU, 7.6 GB RAM, 72 GB disk (address kept out of the
            public repo)
Done by     PyCharm session over SSH, with the owner's go-ahead
Steps
  - apt update/upgrade, then rebooted; automatic security updates on
  - Firewall (ufw): deny incoming except SSH. SSH password login was briefly turned
    off, then restored at the owner's request (they may log in from another machine)
  - Docker 29.8 + Compose from Docker's repository; hello-world OK
  - Repo cloned, development @ 9ada841 (includes #92 dmb- names)
  - .env made from .env.example, chmod 600. EARS_SHARED_SECRET and both database
    passwords generated on the server and never shown. The owner added DISCORD_TOKEN
    and DISCORD_DEV_GUILD_ID. TRANSCRIBER=whisper-local, WHISPER_MODEL=small,
    LOG_FORMAT=json
  - docker compose build (core 853 MB with Whisper, ears 381 MB), then up -d
Result
  postgres healthy; core: "Database updated: 0001_initial, 0002_active_sessions,
  0003_channel_number", Whisper small loaded in ~12 s, connected to Discord, "ears
  connected"; ears: "logged in as DMbot#4185", "connected to core" (a few "core link
  down; retrying" lines first, expected while core loaded Whisper). No errors. No
  ports published to the host.

